  "question": {
    "text": "The area of cross section of the rope used to lift a load by a crane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. The maximum lifting capacity of the crane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> metric tons. To increase the lifting capacity of the crane to 25 metric tons, the required area of cross section of the rope should be<br />(take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
